  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table class=\"MsoTableGrid cke_show_border\" cellspacing=\"0\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\"><strong>RESULT IN IU/mL</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\"><strong>RESULT IN&nbsp;log(IU/mL)</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\"><strong>Analytical Interpretation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">Target not detected</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">Target&nbsp;not detected</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">CMV DNA not detected</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">&lt;50</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">CMV DNA detected, less than 50 IU/ml</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">&gt;=50 to 100000000</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">CMV DNA detected within the linear range&nbsp;of the assay</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">&gt;100000000</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\">CMV DNA detected,greater than &gt;10000000 IU/ml</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Note</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>This test is performed on plasma or serum sample only.</li>\n<li>Linear reporting range of the assay is 50 to 10000000 IU/ml.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Clinical Interpretation</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>A \"Target Not Detected\" result indicates there is no current CMV infection detected in the given sample. If patient tested for viral load assessment, routine clinical &nbsp; follow-up as suggested by the treating clinician.</li>\n<li>CMV DNA detected \"&lt; 50 IU/mL\" result indicates Low-level CMV viremia, may indicate previous spontaneous or treatment-related resolution of CMV infection. Routine clinical follow-up as instructed by the treating clinician is suggested.</li>\n<li>The presence of CMV DNA viral load in the range \"50 to 10000000 IU/mL\" indicates an active infection in the linear range of the test.</li>\n<li>The detection of viral load \"&gt; 10000000 IU/mL\" indicates presence of CMV viral load above upper limit of quantification of the assay.</li>\n<li>The presence of CMV DNA in a sample does not always imply active infection. The diagnosis of CMV infection must be made using a combination of clinical suspicion, physical exam, and detection of the virus.</li>\n<li>The results of this report should be correlated clinically and interpreted in conjunction with the patient &rsquo;s symptoms, history, and other diagnostic information.</li>\n</ol>",
